WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:04.240
Is Moon Knight just another street-level&nbsp;
vigilante in the Marvel universe?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:09.120
Just another superhero? No. Not at all.&nbsp;
Wondering how his multiple personality&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:13.200
disorder and literal god-given powers&nbsp;
give him an advantage? Keep watching!

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:18.240
Marc Spector crossed paths with Khonshu in his&nbsp;
adult life after a botched operation left him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:22.080
near-dead in an African desert. Barely&nbsp;
making it to a mystical Egyptian tomb,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:26.720
Spector passes away at the feet of the moon god's&nbsp;
statue, leading to his spirit meeting Khonshu.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:31.040
The ancient deity saves Spector's life, in&nbsp;
exchange for the mercenary becoming his knight,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:36.640
as Spector himself recounts in "Moon Knight" Vol.&nbsp;
9 #1. This encounter gives birth to the superhero&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:41.600
called Moon Knight and fundamentally changes&nbsp;
not only Spector's life, but his brain as well.

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:45.840
Due to the nature of Khonshu's powers as&nbsp;
a multifaceted, extradimensional entity,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:50.160
his interactions with Spector are said to have&nbsp;
contributed to the fracturing of Spector's psyche.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:52.880
In fact, it has been explained&nbsp;
on more than one occasion that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:56.880
Spector's dissociative identity disorder&nbsp;
may have been a direct result of his mind&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.880 --> 00:01:00.080
attempting to match the complex&nbsp;
nature of the god's own persona.

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:04.720
Furthermore, Spector sometimes possesses the&nbsp;
ability to switch between his personas at will,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:08.000
including Moon Knight himself, which&nbsp;
is actually a separate personality,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:12.560
not just a secret identity. The already formidable&nbsp;
traits that Spector possesses due to his military&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.560 --> 00:01:16.720
background are amplified by the powers of&nbsp;
whichever persona is in charge at the moment.

00:01:17.360 --> 00:01:21.440
For a time, Moon Knight was able to harness&nbsp;
Khonshu's powers in the form of superhuman&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:26.240
strength. According to the "Official Handbook&nbsp;
of the Marvel Universe: Marvel Knights 2005,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.240 --> 00:01:29.840
the Fist of Khonshu's physical strength&nbsp;
increases under the light of the moon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:31.760
peaking during nights with a full moon.

00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:35.920
Interestingly, Moon Knight's strength, speed,&nbsp;
and agility are all affected by the phase of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:41.120
moon — full moon, half-moon, waning or waxing&nbsp;
crescent, or new moon. These fluctuating power&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:44.880
levels are said to be in place because of&nbsp;
Spector's direct ties to both the moon and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:48.640
the Egyptian god. Other guides, such as the&nbsp;
"Official Handbook of the Marvel Universe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.640 --> 00:01:54.640
Deluxe Edition" #9, establish that Spector is&nbsp;
typically capable of bench-pressing 450 pounds.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.640 --> 00:01:59.200
However, he can lift approximately 4,000&nbsp;
pounds when he’s operating under a full moon.

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:03.120
In recent years, however, Moon Knight has had&nbsp;
to deal with the loss of this useful ability,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:07.760
forcing him to push himself to his physical limits&nbsp;
in order to continue his superhero activities.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:12.560
As Spector himself explained in "Moon Knight"&nbsp;
Vol. 5 #9, his super-strength was stripped away&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:15.840
from him by a wrathful Khonshu after&nbsp;
he went against the god's orders.

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:20.800
As Moon Knight can likely attest, the cool&nbsp;
thing about having a god on your side is that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:24.080
for as long as they have a reason to&nbsp;
keep you around, death will be less of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:28.560
a final destination for you and more of a&nbsp;
revolving door. Not that death ever tends&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:32.560
to be permanent in the Marvel universe,&nbsp;
but still. In the case of Moon Knight,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:37.040
this means that unless Khonshu decides to find&nbsp;
a new servant, Spector is functionally immortal.

00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:38.880
“Thanks”

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:44.000
In a discussion with his psychiatrist Dr.&nbsp;
Andrea Sterman in "Moon Knight" Vol. 9 #1,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:48.000
Spector confronts the uncomfortable question&nbsp;
of whether or not he can die with a level of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:52.800
uncertainty. He even recounts that Khonshu&nbsp;
has resurrected him not once, not twice,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:57.840
but at least three times, including when they&nbsp;
met in the Egyptian tomb. Hence, on more than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.840 --> 00:03:02.320
one occasion, Moon Knight has found himself in a&nbsp;
situation where he should have died, but didn't.

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:07.040
That said, Khonshu doesn't seem to have any qualms&nbsp;
about reminding Spector that he is disposable.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:11.760
In "Moon Knight" Vol. 5 #6, during a vision in&nbsp;
which he took the form of Moon Knight's horribly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:16.320
disfigured nemesis Bushman, he took Spector's&nbsp;
life and brought him back just to prove a point.

00:03:17.120 --> 00:03:21.280
While Moon Knight may be functionally immortal,&nbsp;
that doesn't mean that his body is impervious to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.280 --> 00:03:26.080
injury like Luke Cage. In fact, Moon Knight's&nbsp;
battles tend to be extremely brutal, bloody,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.080 --> 00:03:30.400
and violent. They almost always end with both&nbsp;
him and his opponents sustaining broken bones,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:33.840
smashed limbs, massive bleeding,&nbsp;
and other types of physical trauma.

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:42.080
Rather impressively, Spector is able to bear the&nbsp;
extreme pain that comes from his injuries. He has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.080 --> 00:03:46.960
a near-superhuman level of endurance even in the&nbsp;
face of torture from his most sadistic enemies.

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:51.200
Moon Knight's high pain tolerance has been said&nbsp;
to be a combination of his mental state, Khonshu's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:54.960
empowerment, and the sheer amount of physical&nbsp;
abuse he experienced during his time in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:59.760
military. This has led to Spector enduring pain&nbsp;
unlike that of any other street-level superhero.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:05.120
For instance, in "Moon Knight" Vol. 5 #6, Spector&nbsp;
is shown to be basically unaffected by direct&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.120 --> 00:04:09.840
crossbow shots from Taskmaster and is able to&nbsp;
soundly beat his foe despite the severity of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.840 --> 00:04:14.480
his injuries. Six issues later, his crazed&nbsp;
former partner Midnight subjects Spector&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:18.880
to an inhuman level of torture. His limbs&nbsp;
are pinned against a giant clock that digs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:22.720
into his back to systematically remove&nbsp;
Spector's vertebra one bone at a time.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:26.880
Moon Knight endures this pain long&nbsp;
enough to break free from his restraints.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:31.120
He, then, defeats his enemy by ripping off one&nbsp;
of the clock's hands and stabbing him fatally.

00:04:32.240 --> 00:04:37.200
"Avengers" Vol. 8 #33 depicts Moon Knight&nbsp;
during one of his most powerful phases.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:41.760
In an attempt to stop the machinations of the&nbsp;
hellish ruler Mephisto, Khonshu decides that it's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:46.640
time for his earthly avatar to bring about the&nbsp;
Age of Khonshu. He imbues Spector with a host of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.640 --> 00:04:51.840
abilities that the superhero has never possessed&nbsp;
before, a fraction of what Khonshu himself can do.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.840 --> 00:04:55.520
Among the powers that Spector temporarily&nbsp;
receives from the moon god is the ability&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.520 --> 00:04:59.840
to literally control moons and anything&nbsp;
that was made from moon-based materials.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.840 --> 00:05:04.000
This came with the implication that Moon Knight&nbsp;
could also control many other celestial bodies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:07.360
as they are mostly made up of&nbsp;
materials of similar cosmic origin.

00:05:07.360 --> 00:05:12.240
While this power on its own is already impressive,&nbsp;
it also granted Spector a frightening new ability.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:16.160
He could manipulate one of the Marvel&nbsp;
universe's most iconic and fearsome weapons,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.160 --> 00:05:20.880
a tool wielded by another god. Thor's&nbsp;
hammer Mjolnir is made out of Uru,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:26.080
a metal ore reportedly as old as the universe&nbsp;
itself. Since Uru metal is formed in a dying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.080 --> 00:05:30.000
star's heart from material that comes from&nbsp;
a primordial moon, Moon Knight's newfound&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:35.600
lunakinesis allows him to control Thor's weapon,&nbsp;
regardless of his worthiness. Spector demonstrates&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.600 --> 00:05:39.634
this when he makes quick work of the Thunder&nbsp;
God by smacking him around with his own hammer.

00:05:40.596 --> 00:05:41.752
“I knew it.”

00:05:42.261 --> 00:05:46.160
Marc Spector shares his mind-space with&nbsp;
at least four other main personalities,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.160 --> 00:05:49.920
each with their own unique skill sets and&nbsp;
talents reflective of Khonshu's multiple&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.920 --> 00:05:54.080
aspects. Combined with his main persona's&nbsp;
own fighting skills and deductive reasoning,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.080 --> 00:05:57.600
Spector maximizes the talents that each&nbsp;
of his personas brings to the table.

00:05:57.600 --> 00:06:01.280
There is, of course, the Moon Knight persona,&nbsp;
which is said to represent Khonshu's side as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.280 --> 00:06:07.280
the "Watcher of Overnight Travelers," as shown in&nbsp;
"Moon Knight" Vol. 9 #1. Then, there's Mr. Knight,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.280 --> 00:06:12.080
a suave, sharp-dressed consultant who typically&nbsp;
does the talking. There are also two alter-egos&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.080 --> 00:06:16.880
that Spector's psyche developed in his youth:&nbsp;
Steven Grant and Jake Lockley. Grant is depicted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.880 --> 00:06:21.600
as a wealthy public figure and is the persona that&nbsp;
finances Moon Knight's activities. He utilizes and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:21.600 --> 00:06:26.640
grows Spector's wealth to allow him to operate as&nbsp;
a costumed vigilante. Lockley, on the other hand,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.640 --> 00:06:30.960
is a taxi driver who wanders around New York&nbsp;
and gathers intel from street-level sources.

00:06:30.960 --> 00:06:34.480
For a brief time in his career, Spector&nbsp;
was also able to tap into the abilities&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.480 --> 00:06:38.640
of three iconic Avengers… sort of.&nbsp;
As shown in "Moon Knight" Vol. 6 #1,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.640 --> 00:06:42.880
Spector developed the personas of Captain&nbsp;
America, Spider-Man, and Wolverine,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.880 --> 00:06:47.520
and would even occasionally have "meetings" with&nbsp;
them. Whenever each of the personas takes control,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:47.520 --> 00:06:51.520
Spector even equips himself with the appropriate&nbsp;
gear to mimic their iconic move sets.

00:06:52.560 --> 00:06:56.560
Yet another example of a short-lived but&nbsp;
spectacular power in Moon Knight's arsenal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.560 --> 00:07:01.680
was shown in "Avengers" Vol. 8 #33. After&nbsp;
being allowed to tap into the vast reserves&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:01.680 --> 00:07:05.680
of Khonshu's might, Moon Knight gained the&nbsp;
ability to absorb the powers of his opponents&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.680 --> 00:07:10.720
via mystical artifacts. However, his impressive&nbsp;
absorption abilities also had their limits.

00:07:10.720 --> 00:07:14.720
Moon Knight first puts this ability to the&nbsp;
test in a confrontation with the Iron Fist,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.720 --> 00:07:20.000
Danny Rand. After subduing Iron Fist with a&nbsp;
barrage of Khonshu-powered attacks, Spector whips&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:25.040
out a divine ankh, which he uses to steal the&nbsp;
power of the immortal dragon residing within Rand.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:25.040 --> 00:07:30.080
Using the ankhs and a bit of necromancy, Moon&nbsp;
Knight easily defeats Doctor Strange as well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:30.080 --> 00:07:34.560
and brazenly takes control of Ghost&nbsp;
Rider Robbie Reyes' Spirit of Vengeance.

00:07:34.560 --> 00:07:38.960
However, the ankhs were of virtually no help to&nbsp;
Moon Knight when he went up against Wakanda's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.960 --> 00:07:43.200
T'Challa, revealing their limitations.&nbsp;
As Black Panther's powers were granted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.200 --> 00:07:47.473
by the heart-shaped herb he'd consumed, Moon&nbsp;
Knight could not use the ankhs to steal them.

00:07:47.473 --> 00:07:49.140
“Wakanda forever!”

00:07:50.960 --> 00:07:53.760
While Moon Knight has sported quite&nbsp;
a few different looks over the course&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.760 --> 00:07:58.400
of his costumed career, his most iconic&nbsp;
ensemble remains his all-white hooded suit.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.400 --> 00:08:01.520
And while they may not look like they&nbsp;
offer much in the way of protection,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:01.520 --> 00:08:06.400
Spector's assorted outfits are actually designed&nbsp;
to be as resistant and durable as their wearer.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:06.400 --> 00:08:09.840
They're also all white, of course,&nbsp;
as Moon Knight prioritizes shock&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:09.840 --> 00:08:14.160
value and intimidation over the element of&nbsp;
surprise when it comes to subduing perps.

00:08:14.160 --> 00:08:18.560
Spector's early suits include Kevlar vests,&nbsp;
as well as a host of defensive and offensive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:18.560 --> 00:08:22.800
features. Later on, Moon Knight would tweak&nbsp;
his getup to offer even more protection,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.800 --> 00:08:27.200
infusing the design with Carbonadium.&nbsp;
In the Marvel universe, Carbonadium is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:27.200 --> 00:08:32.560
described as a flexible material comparable to&nbsp;
Adamantium in terms of quality and durability.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:32.560 --> 00:08:36.720
You may know Adamantium as the material&nbsp;
that coats Wolverine’s bones and Carbonadium&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:36.720 --> 00:08:40.000
from its heavy use in X-Men villain&nbsp;
Omega Red’s tentacles. Moon Knight&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:40.000 --> 00:08:44.480
also wears a long cape that enables him to catch&nbsp;
updrafts and glide across limited distances,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.480 --> 00:08:48.800
as well as metal bracers on his arms. Some&nbsp;
of Moon Knight's most recognizable weapons&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.800 --> 00:08:53.840
include his crescent moon-shaped throwing&nbsp;
blades and his adamantium-laced bo staff.

00:08:53.840 --> 00:08:55.920
Incredibly, the one thing about Moon Knight that

00:08:55.920 --> 00:08:59.600
many may perceive as a disadvantage has&nbsp;
proven to be the superhero's strongest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:59.600 --> 00:09:03.120
line of defense against some of the&nbsp;
Marvel universe's greatest minds.

00:09:03.120 --> 00:09:06.320
Due to Spector's mental state, the&nbsp;
white-clad crime fighter has developed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:06.320 --> 00:09:11.280
a powerful resistance against various forms of&nbsp;
psychic attacks and attempts at mind control.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.280 --> 00:09:14.720
His mental resilience also makes it&nbsp;
tremendously difficult for telepathic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:14.720 --> 00:09:18.720
individuals to read his mind, effectively&nbsp;
deterring them from anticipating his next&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:18.720 --> 00:09:21.120
move or discerning what his true objectives are.

00:09:21.120 --> 00:09:24.880
Moon Knight doesn't take too&nbsp;
kindly to mental invaders. In fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:24.880 --> 00:09:30.560
as "Moon Knight" Vol 9 #2 shows, his mind can&nbsp;
be a very hostile place for unwelcome visitors.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:30.560 --> 00:09:35.280
While facing off against a criminal telepath named&nbsp;
Hawley, Moon Knight was able to overpower his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:35.280 --> 00:09:39.760
adversary almost as soon as he invaded. Spector&nbsp;
himself claims that his direct interactions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:39.760 --> 00:09:44.480
with Khonshu have turned his mind into "poisoned&nbsp;
ground." The villain was thoroughly overwhelmed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:44.480 --> 00:09:48.720
by Moon Knight's sheer mental fortitude and&nbsp;
was rendered catatonic after their encounter.

00:09:49.520 --> 00:09:52.000
While he generally doesn't&nbsp;
have access to this ability,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:52.000 --> 00:09:55.840
Moon Knight was once able to wield&nbsp;
complete control over his physical form.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:55.840 --> 00:10:00.320
This includes the ability to pass right through&nbsp;
otherwise impassable objects, as well as being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:00.320 --> 00:10:04.800
able to survive in places without an Earth-like&nbsp;
atmosphere for extended periods of time.

00:10:04.800 --> 00:10:09.680
In "Conan: Serpent War" #4, Moon Knight finds&nbsp;
himself temporarily time-displaced. Upon his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:09.680 --> 00:10:13.520
return to the present day, Spector discovers that&nbsp;
he is able to pass through the glass pane of his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:13.520 --> 00:10:18.480
residence, transforming into his costumed&nbsp;
alter upon stepping out. This power boost,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:18.480 --> 00:10:22.960
which was granted by Khonshu to enable his&nbsp;
servant to complete a series of complicated tasks,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:22.960 --> 00:10:28.720
is also seen on full display in "Avengers" Vol. 8&nbsp;
#33. As Moon Knight himself observes, he is able&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:28.720 --> 00:10:35.040
to ride Ghost Rider's flaming 1969 Dodge Charger&nbsp;
and even battle Thor in outer space without dying.

